54
00:02:53.683 --> 00:02:57.169
Grammar focus: Gerund phrases for advice.

55
00:02:57.469 --> 00:02:58.633
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:01.804
Practicing regularly builds confidence.

57
00:03:02.717 --> 00:03:05.343
Making eye contact connects you with the audience.

58
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.691
Preparing your notes helps you stay calm.

59
00:03:09.633 --> 00:03:15.560
A gerund phrase can be the subject. It takes a singular verb: Practicing builds…, not Practicing build…

60
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:20.478
Be careful! Don't say: Practice regularly builds confidence.

61
00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:25.571
Say: Practicing regularly builds confidence.

62
00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:28.172
A gerund phrase starts with the -ing form.

63
